WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.469
President Trump's
former confidant Omarosa

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:05.405
now claims that Trump
knew in advance

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.506
about the Democratic e-mails
Russia hacked

00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:09.242
during the 2016 campaign.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.544
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:12.912
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.882 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.084
It's important to remember
that any time you hear

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.386
the President or his defenders
say anything

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:23.155
about the Russia probe,
they don't actually care about

00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:26.325
the details of the case or
the legal principles at stake.

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:29.195
Their sole motivation is
to discredit the investigation

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.663
in the minds of voters.

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:33.666
Trump's lawyer Rudy Giuliani
even admitted as much on Sunday.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:36.135
-Why have you decided to

00:00:36.135 --> 00:00:38.437
literally try this case

00:00:38.437 --> 00:00:39.572
in the court of public opinion?

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.107
Is that a deliberate strategy

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.408
on your part?
-Yeah, absolutely deliberate.

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:43.676
I mean,
that's where it's being tried.

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.044
Public opinion will be,

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.645
as you know, very important.

00:00:46.645 --> 00:00:48.347
When I came into the case,

00:00:48.347 --> 00:00:50.316
public opinion was against us.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:51.584
Think of it this way --

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.987
They're our Grand Jury.

00:00:53.987 --> 00:00:56.222
-You think the public
is your jury?

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:59.259
Oh, I have bad news because
you know who's your jury?

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:00.193
The jury.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:01.527
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.527 --> 00:01:03.362
When you're in the court room
and the foreman says,

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:04.863
"We find the defendant guilty,"

00:01:04.863 --> 00:01:06.399
you're not going to be able
to turn around and say,

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.767
"Now let's hear from you,
America.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:11.236 line:0%
Text 555-0100 for 'not guilty!'"

00:01:11.236 --> 00:01:12.672 line:0%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:15.541
So Giuliani admitted it.

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:18.077
For Trump and his team, it's not
about the facts of the case.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:19.212
It's about public opinion.

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.914
That's why Rudy's on TV
all the time

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:25.218
looking like he just saw
a spider on his toothbrush.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.419
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.888
That may also be why Rudy
seems so uninterested

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.389
in the actual work
of being a lawyer.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:32.725
Like, you know, researching
basic legal questions

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.028
or looking over documents.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.998 line:0%
-Of course it's a crime.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:41.667 line:0%
No, under article 2
of the Constitution,

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.302 line:0%
I'm not going to tell you
my opinion on it

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:44.937 line:0%
because I haven't really gotten

00:01:44.937 --> 00:01:46.506 line:0%
to the conclusion
of researching it.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:49.208
-Is it possible that
Robert Mueller has something

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.376
and you have no idea
what he has?

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:51.611
-No.
-Why?

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.712
-Because I've been
through everything.

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:54.146
I've talked to the President.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:55.248
The President is an honest man.

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.149
The President did nothing wrong,

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:57.382
hasn't done anything wrong.

00:01:57.382 --> 00:01:59.018
Throughout this, he said,

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.786
"Give them all the documents."

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:02.054
John Dowd will tell you this.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:03.655
1.4 million documents.

00:02:03.655 --> 00:02:05.524
We didn't even look at them.
We just gave it to him.

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.527
-You didn't even look at them?!

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:08.461
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.629
You're his lawyer!

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.898
You should probably know
what you're handing over.

00:02:11.898 --> 00:02:13.666
"We gave Mueller everything.

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:17.303
Trump's schedule, his e-mails,
his tax returns -- Oh, no!"

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:20.039
Oh, the tax returns!

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.508
Oh, Rudy,
you screwed up this time!

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:23.242
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.144
Ohh!

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:27.647
Oh, Rudy!

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.982
[ Sighs ]

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:31.050
I'm going to brush my teeth
to clear my head.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:31.951
Spider!"

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:34.920
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.989
Rudy's lack of preparation
might explain

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:39.792
why he can't seem to settle
on one coherent argument

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.093
about what actually happened.

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.229
For example, Robert Mueller
wants to ask Trump

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.532
about his conversation
with then-FBI director

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:48.100
James Comey who claims
Trump told him

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.870
to drop his investigation
of ex-National Security Advisor

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.670
Michael Flynn.

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.472
Rudy keeps cycling through

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.474
different explanations
for that conversation,

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:56.843
sometimes in the same interview

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.477
as he did Monday
on "Fox &amp; Friends."

00:02:58.477 --> 00:02:59.879
-Here's what happened.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.714
The President says, "I never
said to Flynn anything about --"

00:03:02.714 --> 00:03:03.449
-"I never said to Comey."

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.483
-"I never said to Comey

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:06.618
anything about Flynn."
Comey says,

00:03:06.618 --> 00:03:08.321
and he adds this
at the very end,

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.489
Comey says,
"He told me to see if --

00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:12.959
if I can give him a break."
Basically.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:16.162
So we have three defenses
to that.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:18.230
Under article 2
of the Constitution,

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.698
you can't really question

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:21.200
why the President
would say something.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.534
He has the power to say it.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:26.839
Number two, what he was saying
is perfectly justifiable.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.108
He didn't say, "You must,
you have to,

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.576
I'll fire you if you don't."

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:32.077
He said, "Consider it."

00:03:32.077 --> 00:03:34.013
Number three, he never said it.

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.014
-Oh, my God!

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.216
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.216 --> 00:03:40.286
He's like a [bleep] magician
frantically asking,

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.687
"is this your card?
No? Okay.

00:03:41.687 --> 00:03:43.021
How about this one?
Okay. Hold on.

00:03:43.021 --> 00:03:44.156
There's 50 more. Okay.

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:45.825
Is it a red one?
Is it a red one?

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:49.128
Does it start with
a fo-- sev-- nine?

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.064
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:53.566
Rudy clearly just makes stuff up
as he goes along,

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:54.834
and now he's got a new line.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.835
He's telling people
that Mueller told him

00:03:56.835 --> 00:03:59.805
he would wrap up the
investigation by September 1st,

00:03:59.805 --> 00:04:02.608
although Rudy's story
doesn't sound very convincing.

00:04:02.608 --> 00:04:03.909
-We think it should end.

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:05.845
-The whole investigation?

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.179
-Absolutely.
It should be terminated.

00:04:07.179 --> 00:04:08.548
He should put out his report,

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:10.283
tell the American people
what he has.

00:04:10.283 --> 00:04:12.151
Why did I say September 1st?

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.353
Because a long time ago,

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.787
two months ago
when we met with him,

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:17.456
he threw out September 1st
as a date that he might be able

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:19.158
to get the report done by.
-Hmm.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.359
-And --

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:21.728
-Does he still sound like that?

00:04:21.728 --> 00:04:22.895
-Well, we haven't talked --

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:24.797
he has not repeated that
since then.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.699
But he hasn't taken it back.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.434
-Oh, he hasn't taken it back?

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:31.004
You're representing the
President of the United States,

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:34.140
and you're handling this case
like a fifth grader playing tag.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.141
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:37.676
"You said September 1st!
No backsies!

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:39.645
Now pick one of these words."

00:04:39.645 --> 00:04:42.581
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:47.419
But if Rudy seems unequipped --

00:04:47.419 --> 00:04:49.188
if Rudy seems at all unequipped

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.057
to handle the Russia
investigation so far,

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.092
then he's really going to be
in over his head this week

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.561
with the latest revelations
from Trump's former confidant

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:57.830
and aide
Omarosa Manigault-Newman.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.900
Omarosa's tell-all book has
a lot of sensational allegations

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.603
like her claim that she saw
Trump put a note in his mouth.

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:09.541
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.541 --> 00:05:11.811
Now this is Omarosa
we're talking about.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:14.947
So anything she says should be
taken with a grain of lithium.

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.115
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.318
But yesterday she dropped
a new bombshell

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:20.185
claiming that Trump
knew in advance

00:05:20.185 --> 00:05:21.587
about the Hillary Clinton
e-mails

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.456
that Russia hacked
during the campaign.

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:25.758
-I think that he should come
clean with the American people.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:27.192
I think that he should honest

00:05:27.192 --> 00:05:28.727
about what he did during

00:05:28.727 --> 00:05:30.697
the campaign and what he

00:05:30.697 --> 00:05:32.030
continued to do
in the White House.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:33.899
-You were instructed,
according to your book,

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:36.969
to bring up the e-mails
at every point you could

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.237
at the end of the 2016 campaign?

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:40.005
-That's correct.
-Hillary Clinton's e-mails.

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:41.140
-Yes, that was our talker.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.508
-Did Donald Trump know about

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:43.943
those e-mails
before they came out?

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:44.844
-Absolutely.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:46.045
-He knew about them?
-Yes.

00:05:46.045 --> 00:05:47.146
-He knew what was coming out

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:49.081
before WikilLeaks released them?
-Yes.

00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:52.851
-Amazing. So after Trump's
public praise of Vladimir Putin,

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:54.720
his attorney general's meetings
with Russians,

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:56.455
his campaign chairman's
money laundering,

00:05:56.455 --> 00:05:58.391
his deputy campaign chairman's
tax fraud,

00:05:58.391 --> 00:06:00.493
his personal fixer's
secret shell company,

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:02.928
his national security advisor's
lies to the FBI,

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:05.331
his son's attempt to get dirt
from a foreign adversary

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:06.999
and son-in-law's
secret back channels

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:08.133
with that adversary,

00:06:08.133 --> 00:06:09.769
the person who could end up
taking down

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:12.738
the President
of the United States is Omarosa.

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:14.707
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.975
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.975 --> 00:06:20.379
Omarosa.

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:22.648
It took her 14 years,

00:06:22.648 --> 00:06:25.384
but she's finally getting
revenge for Trump firing her

00:06:25.384 --> 00:06:26.519
in season one.

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:27.786
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.786 --> 00:06:29.388
Now, let's be honest --
the only fitting way

00:06:29.388 --> 00:06:31.957
for this presidency to end
would be Trump to get indicted

00:06:31.957 --> 00:06:34.594
and leave the White House
crying in the back of a cab.

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:36.061
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.061 --> 00:06:39.198
Omarosa has also written in
her book that Trump was furious

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:42.434
at his son Don Jr. after Don Jr.
released his e-mails

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:45.537
with Russians revealing that
the infamous Trump Tower meeting

00:06:45.537 --> 00:06:49.174
in 2016 was an attempt to get
dirt on Hillary Clinton.

00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:50.843
That contradicted
their original story

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.778
that the meeting was about
adoption policy.

00:06:52.778 --> 00:06:55.014
Omarosa writes...

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:07.359
Wait, so he just said this in
passing during a conversation?

00:07:07.359 --> 00:07:10.763
Can you imagine making small
talk with Trump in the elevator?

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:12.598
"Hey, Donald.
Hot enough for you?"

00:07:12.598 --> 00:07:14.233
[ As Trump ]
"My son's an ass[bleep]"

00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:18.637
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.637 --> 00:07:20.973
[ Normal voice ]
Now, Omarosa obviously has

00:07:20.973 --> 00:07:23.176
as much credibility
as anyone else in Trump World,

00:07:23.176 --> 00:07:25.077
which is to say very little.

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:26.779
But she's been releasing
secret tapes

00:07:26.779 --> 00:07:28.814
of her conversations to back up
her side of the story.

00:07:28.814 --> 00:07:32.184
In fact, she's taped everyone
from John Kelly to Ivanka Trump

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:33.919
to Jared Kushner
to the President himself,

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:36.855
which is incredible given that,
as we've noted before,

00:07:36.855 --> 00:07:40.159
Trump has a lifelong obsession
with being secretly taped.

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:42.161
We saw that shortly after
he became President

00:07:42.161 --> 00:07:45.297
when he falsely accused Obama
of tapping his wires

00:07:45.297 --> 00:07:47.967
and then angrily tried to
storm out of an interview

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:50.536
when he was asked to provide
evidence for that claim.

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:53.739
-Did President Obama give you
any advice that was helpful?

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:54.574
That you think,
wow, he really --

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:55.808
-Well, was very nice to me.

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:57.776
But after that,
we've had some difficulties.

00:07:57.776 --> 00:07:59.311
So it doesn't matter.

00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:01.847
You know, words are less
important to me than deeds.

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:03.883
And you saw what happened
with surveillance.

00:08:03.883 --> 00:08:05.417
-But you stand by that claim
about him?

00:08:05.417 --> 00:08:07.185
-I don't stand by anything.
I just --

00:08:07.185 --> 00:08:08.587
You can take it
the way you want.

00:08:08.587 --> 00:08:12.658
I think that is a very big
surveillance of our citizens.

00:08:12.658 --> 00:08:15.061
I think it's a very big topic.

00:08:15.061 --> 00:08:17.296
And it's a topic that should
be number one

00:08:17.296 --> 00:08:20.265
and we should find out
what the hell is going on.

00:08:20.265 --> 00:08:22.367
I have my own opinions.
You can have your own opinions.

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:23.536
-But I want to know
your opinions.

00:08:23.536 --> 00:08:24.603
You're the President
of the United States.

00:08:24.603 --> 00:08:25.537
-Okay. That's enough.

00:08:25.537 --> 00:08:28.307
Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:33.312
[ Laughter ]

00:08:35.881 --> 00:08:37.783
[ Laughter ]

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:39.985
-[ As Trump ]
"Now if you'll excuse me,

00:08:39.985 --> 00:08:42.455
I have a lot of paperwork
to eat."

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:48.727
[ Laughter ]

00:08:48.727 --> 00:08:50.963
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:57.836 --> 00:09:00.172
[ Normal voice ] Trump
surrounded himself with grifters

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:02.942
and con artists, and now that
it's coming back to haunt him,

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:04.677
he's trying to grift his way
out of it.

00:09:04.677 --> 00:09:06.378
It's the first rule of Trumpism.

00:09:06.378 --> 00:09:08.413
Everyone is grifting
everyone else

00:09:08.413 --> 00:09:10.650
and everyone eventually
turns on Trump.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.484
Omarosa is just
the latest example.

00:09:12.484 --> 00:09:14.754
They're all following
the Trump mantra which is...

00:09:14.754 --> 00:09:16.121
-I don't stand by anything.

00:09:16.121 --> 00:09:18.190
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.692
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:19.692 --> 00:09:21.861 line:0%
♪♪

